  "Question": "Triangle \\(ABC\\) has a right angle at \\(C.\\) If \\(\\sin A=\\frac23,\\) then \\(\\tan B\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac35\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt5}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt5}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac53\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(C\\) is the right angle, \\(AB\\) is the hypotenuse, and\n\\[\n\\sin A=\\frac{BC}{AB}=\\frac23.\n\\]\nThus we can write \\(BC=2t\\) and \\(AB=3t\\) for some \\(t>0\\). The Pythagorean theorem finds the other leg:\n\\[\nAC^2=(3t)^2-(2t)^2=5t^2.\n\\]\nSide lengths are positive, so \\(AC=t\\sqrt5\\). For angle \\(B\\), the opposite leg is \\(AC\\) and the adjacent leg is \\(BC\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\tan B=\\frac{AC}{BC}=\\frac{t\\sqrt5}{2t}=\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}},\n\\]\nchoice D.",
